,"best","best","best","best","best","excellent","good","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent"],"moments":[{"ply":31,"name":"16.Bxe7","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"16.Bxe7 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 57% to 26%.","points":["Black answers 16…Nxe3, which takes the queen on e3.","After Nxe3, Black wins 5 points of material within 7 moves.","Better was 16.Nxd5 (+0.80), which takes the knight on d5."],"better":"16.Nxd5 stops …Nxe3. After 16…Nxd5 17.Bxd5 Bxh4 18.Bb3 a5 19.g3, the knights are traded (+0.80)."},{"ply":61,"name":"31.Ra2","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"31.Ra2 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 69% to 24%.","points":["Black answers 31…Bc4: the bishop forks the rook and the knight: both can't be saved at once.","After Bc4, Black wins 2 points of material within 5 moves.","Better was 31.Nc7 (+2.21), which attacks the rook on e8."],"better":"31.Nc7 wins the exchange, picking it up with 32.Nxe8. After 31…Bd7 32.Nxe8 Bxe8 33.d5 Bb5 34.d6, White comes out two pawns up (+2.21)."},{"ply":96,"name":"48…Be6+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"48…Be6+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The bishop joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the White king.","Moves the attacked bishop to safety.","The next best move, 48…Bb3, would drop Black's winning chances from 50% to 24% (+3.17).","48…Be6+ joins the attack on the king and saves the attacked bishop.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","White answers 49.Kg3."]},{"ply":99,"name":"50.Kf4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"50.Kf4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Protects the knight on e3, which was hanging.","The next best move, 50.Nf1, would drop White's winning chances from 51% to 23% (−3.25).","50.Kf4 stops …Rxe3.","Black was threatening …Rxe3, winning a knight. Kf4 takes care of it.","Black answers 50…Rd2.","Engine line: 50…Rd2 51.Bc5 Ba2 52.c4 Kg8 53.Ba7 (+0.04)."]},{"ply":102,"name":"51…fxg5+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"51…fxg5+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the pawn on g5.","The next best move, 51…Kg6, would drop Black's winning chances from 48% to 29% (+2.39).","51…fxg5+ wins a pawn.","Takes the g5 pawn and wins a pawn once the captures settle.","White answers 52.Ke4.","Engine line: 52.Ke4 Ba2 53.d5 Bxd5+ 54.Kd3 Rxe3+ 55.Kxe3 g4 56.fxg4 hxg4 57.g3 (+0.20)."]},{"ply":106,"name":"53…Rxg2","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"53…Rxg2 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 47% to 10%.","points":["White answers 54.Nxg2, which takes the rook on g2.","After Nxg2, White wins 5 points of material within 2 moves.","Better was 53…Rd2 (+0.34): the rook takes the half-open d-file."],"better":"53…Rd2 takes the half-open d-file. After 54.c4 Bxc4 55.Nxc4 Rxg2 56.d5 h3, Black is a pawn down (+0.34)."},{"ply":109,"name":"55.Bd6","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"55.Bd6!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the knight on g2 where it can be taken.","Black can take, but after 55…hxg2 56.Bh2 Bc4 57.d5 the engine rates it +5.62.","55.Bd6 prepares Bh2 and d5.","The engine's plan continues with Bh2 and d5: this move is the first step.","Black answers 55…hxg2, winning a knight.","After 55…hxg2 56.Bh2 Bc4 57.d5 Bf1 58.Kd4, White is a piece down (+5.62)."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"55.Bd6!! leaves the knight on g2 hanging. Taking it gives White an attack worth more than the knight."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"The knight on g2 is attacked by the h3 pawn, and 55.Bd6 doesn't save it. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"If Black takes the knight","text":"55…hxg2 is met by 56.Bh2. Then 57.fxg4 takes the g4 pawn, and 58.Ke5 threatens Kxe6, winning a bishop. White is still a piece down, but the attack is worth more: White is clearly better (+2.75). This is Black's best try."},{"title":"Why not save the knight first?","text":"Saving it with 55.Ne3, the best way to do that, is clearly weaker (−5.66 against +5.62). Black answers 55…h2, pushing the passed pawn to h2. That would leave White losing."}]},{"ply":111,"name":"56.Bh2","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"56.Bh2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 56.d5, would drop White's winning chances from 91% to 7% (−6.90).","56.Bh2 prepares d5 and c4.","The engine's plan continues with d5 and c4: this move is the first step.","Black answers 56…Kg7.","Engine line: 56…Kg7 57.d5 Bf7 58.c4 Kf8 59.c5 (+6.11)."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Gambit Declined: Janowski Variation","eco":"D31","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 6…Be7: 12 moves in all, 6 by White and 6 by Black.","Theory runs out after 6…Be7: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}